{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e1a2b3c4-1111-4a2b-9c3d-a1b2c3d4e5f6",
    "name": "TrainTrack",
    "description": "Collection for the TrainTrack backend (all 10 phases). Works either way: import just this file and every value falls back to a collection variable with a sensible default, or also import TrainTrack.postman_environment.json and select it (top-right environment dropdown) to see the values in the more familiar environment view instead — login requests write the tokens they capture to both places, so either works.\n\nBefore running anything:\n1. `docker compose up -d` (Postgres, Kafka, LocalStack)\n2. Start core-api (`./mvnw -pl traintrack-core-api -am spring-boot:run`, :8080) and, if you want the Audit Service folder to return anything, audit-service too (:8081)\n3. Run the four requests in **Auth** first (Acme Admin, Trainer, Employee, Beta Admin) — everything else reuses the tokens they capture. Easiest way: open the collection's \"...\" menu → Run collection, and run the whole thing top to bottom once.\n\nSeeded users (all passwords `password123`): admin@acme.test (ADMIN), trainer@acme.test (TRAINER), employee@acme.test (EMPLOYEE), admin@beta.test (ADMIN, a *different* organisation — used here to demonstrate tenant isolation).\n\nNotes:\n- **Idempotency-Key**: enrolment creation requires this header. The collection uses a fixed `idempotencyKey` variable on purpose — resend \"Create Enrolment\" unchanged to see the exact same response come back instead of a new enrolment (see \"Create Enrolment — Replay Same Idempotency Key\"). Change that variable to a fresh UUID first if you actually want to create another one.\n- **AI Assistant**: needs a real `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` configured on core-api or you'll get a clean 502 (`AssistantUnavailableException`) — that's the app working as designed against a missing/invalid key, not a broken request. It's also rate-limited (`ASSISTANT_RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS`, default 20/hour/user).\n- **Bulk Enrolment**: the \"file\" form-data field needs a file attached manually (Postman can't ship an embedded file in a portable collection) — use `postman/sample-bulk-enrolment.csv` from the repo, or any CSV with a `userId,courseId` header.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "coreApiUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "auditServiceUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8081" },

    { "key": "seedPassword", "value": "password123" },
    { "key": "acmeAdminEmail", "value": "admin@acme.test" },
    { "key": "trainerEmail", "value": "trainer@acme.test" },
    { "key": "employeeEmail", "value": "employee@acme.test" },
    { "key": "betaAdminEmail", "value": "admin@beta.test" },

    { "key": "acmeOrgId", "value": "a0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
    { "key": "betaOrgId", "value": "a0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
    { "key": "acmeAdminId", "value": "d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
    { "key": "trainerId", "value": "d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
    { "key": "employeeId", "value": "d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003" },
    { "key": "betaAdminId", "value": "d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004" },
    { "key": "seedCourseId", "value": "e0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },

    { "key": "idempotencyKey", "value": "b3b6a1d2-0000-4000-8000-000000000001" },

    { "key": "acmeAdminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "acmeAdminRefreshToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "trainerToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employeeToken", "value": "" },
